  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The announcement of the Gospel. SEQUÉNTIA, from sequor, is the continuation: the passage read follows on in the Gospel, as distinct from INÍTIUM, its beginning. It is the nominative of a heading, with no verb expressed or understood. SANCTI agrees with EVANGÉLII; SECÚNDUM with the accusative names the evangelist.",
    "source": {
      "method": "The Latin follows the Benziger Brothers 1962 editio iuxta typicam, which prints this heading over the Gospel on printed p. 336 (IA leaf n417 / PDF p. 418) and over the 29 further readings named in the witness header; it is compared with the heading line of the pinned Divinum Officium file that the reading's own digital witness binds. Source review remains pending.",
